<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>3 years on, Morocco earthquake victims still wait for help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd5d0eb1d16dd6a61a0422bba2fbed8ac033d522d88f0d9092dcb5bdca62054</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844--12aebab2298e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reconstruction has progressed in the three years since the 2023 Morocco earthquake, but some survivors are still living in tents. Locals are divided as to how successful it's been, and whether state aid is enough.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ecf80da667eb3a8be4aad1ab557ee5513c47476f1b3df4d6a27501688f5cc3e</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cf4636c25c253204212c390cc4c842523c9872f27a70998fbac55a25ab2dcf5</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Can creating new provinces fix governance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3659f2782c5ad29c473a364f0f99b83eaa3c8a1d2f4f6ea0509007fc3cd41844</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059--3974ef70363a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistanis broadly agree that the country needs more responsive and effective government, but many question whether simply creating more provinces is the solution.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Threatening letters revive fears among Kashmiri Pandits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1211b1dcb5a6f0a092ebe6d311ee00574bb0a82d42fe1080fa98e699b7d39c</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481--ac4e07371076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaked addresses and phone numbers have reignited fears among Hindu government employees who returned to Muslim-majority Kashmir under a rehabilitation scheme.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b9cb1112024ae2953cdd27f6bf5c3cf7e46861ad850edba3b9f867d6d7eee2</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c913d7cd0e83a8dc9fe505243e582fef7c73b3212f4031f9072eea2c885115dd</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change and food insecurity could fuel future conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c5fbf0b2d2683c397926d651dbcdc473bd4a6395304312ad305c7faa3fc1321</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431--8e63f64c4115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change, conflict, and trade tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why children are last to be treated in medical crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dda8a68e23dab0b78947efb8108815edb9e8b68fd1cc1b152a2bad3b773f624c</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107--c059b44b485e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo, children are more likely to die than adults. But it's not always due to the disease. Specific medicines for younger people are often harder to come by.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00f147cfeeda928286af830e7e33232eab3af7acc9cda4c7c760580e8484948</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why many Syrians feel Assad death sentence isn't enough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1efb98569ac8bf0a0290343002f84d51a3182134346180099829cc0d219fd610</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915--4ab418802105.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In July, a Syrian court sentenced former dictator Bashar Assad to death for crimes against his own people. But after 14 years of civil war, many survivors are demanding more when it comes to transitional justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d93e193f1aa0443bf0d750198f587a3947112c4903b99ac8670eaddb0d2f395e</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
